        "senderName": "NWS Baltimore MD/Washington DC",
        "headline": "Flood Watch issued August 11 at 2:06AM EDT until August 12 at 5:00AM EDT by NWS Baltimore MD/Washington DC",
        "description": "Repetitive rounds of precipitation through tonight will raise\nflash flood potential.\n\n* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is possible.\n\n* WHERE...A portion of western Maryland, including the following\nareas, Eastern Garrett and Western Garrett.\n\n* WHEN...Through late tonight.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- While most locations will generally see less than 2 inches of\nrainfall, isolated locations could see up to 2 to 4 inches,\nwhich would create high water issues through portions of far\nwestern Maryland.\n- Please visit www.weather.gov/safety/flood for flood safety\nand preparedness information",
        "instruction": "You should monitor later forecasts and be alert for possible Flood\nWarnings. Those living in areas prone to flooding should be prepared\nto take action should flooding develop.",
        "response": "Prepare",
